<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/532">532 CE</a><a href="/years/533">533 CE</a><a href="/years/534">534 CE</a><a href="/years/535">535 CE</a><a href="/years/537" aria-current="page">537 CE</a><a href="/years/541">541 CE</a><a href="/years/546">546 CE</a><a href="/years/547">547 CE</a><a href="/years/552">552 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belisarius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-2">2 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">King Vitiges and the Ostrogoths begin the siege of Rome</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A numerically superior Ostrogothic army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/witigis">Vitiges</a> laid siege to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, held by Byzantine forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a>, who with his bucellarii was almost cut off outside the Flaminian Gate. The year-long siege shaped the rest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554">Gothic War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554">Gothic War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-27">27 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Justinian dedicates Hagia Sophia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Justinian dedicated the new church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, built in under six years. It was the world's largest cathedral for nearly a thousand years and later served as a mosque and a museum.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-shayuan">Battle of Shayuan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Shayuan was fought in 537 between the Eastern Wei under Gao Huan and the Western Wei under Yuwen Tai, near the Wei River in modern Shaanxi.</p></div></li></ol></section>
